## Facts

- **Stack:** Drupal 11 backend (`drupal/`, PHP {{ runtime.php_version }}, MariaDB {{ runtime.db_version }}) + Nuxt 4 frontend (`frontend/`, Bun runtime) with the [Blökkli](https://docs.blokk.li/) visual editor. The frontend does **all** public rendering and consumes Drupal via GraphQL — Drupal is only reachable on specific paths (admin, GraphQL), so public-facing features belong in Nuxt.
- **Local dev** runs entirely inside [DDEV](https://ddev.readthedocs.io/){% if deployment == "platform.sh" %}; remote environments run on [Platform.sh/Upsun](https://fixed.docs.upsun.com/) — only `main` deploys to production{% endif %}.
- **URLs:** local `https://{{ name }}.ddev.site/`{% if deployment == "platform.sh" %}, live {{ url }}/{% endif %}.
- **ICMS is consumed, not developed here:** `iqual/icms_*` (Composer) and `@iqual/nuxt-icms-*` (NPM) are upstream dependencies with constraints frozen to the tested release. Don't hand-loosen their version constraints or patch them locally — see the `icms-update` and `drupal-contrib` skills.
- **Config is code:** Drupal config lives in `drupal/config/` — export with `ddev drush cex`, import with `ddev drush cim`, never hand-edit it in a target environment. `ddev drush deploy` is the canonical post-change sequence (`updb` → `cim` → `deploy:hook` → `cr`).
- **Stale caches:** after backend changes run `ddev drush cr`; restart the frontend dev server if HMR looks stale.
- **Workflow:** GitHub Flow — branch → PR → human-approved review → merge. Branch format `issue/XXX-YYY_description`, commit format `XXX-YYY: Description`, referencing a Jira issue. **Never push to `main`, and never merge a PR yourself.**

## Commands

Everything runs through DDEV — **never run `composer`, `drush`, `bun`, or `npm` without the `ddev` prefix**, the native tool won't use the container. The **Makefile is the source of truth** — run `make help` for the full list. The runtime is usually already up: check with `ddev drush status`, and don't run `make install` unless explicitly asked to (re)provision.

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Check site state | `ddev drush status` |
| Start local runtime | `make runtime` |
| Build & deploy both stacks | `make stack` (= `make drupal` + `make frontend`) |
| Nuxt dev server with HMR | `make frontend` (foreground; `make install` already starts it — don't run it twice) |
| Run tests | `make test` (PHPUnit + Vitest) |
| Lint / auto-fix | `make lint` / `make beauty` |
| Install an ICMS bundle | `make bundle-<name>` (Drupal side first, then frontend — the target orders this correctly) |
{% if deployment == "platform.sh" %}
| Pull config from remote | `make config-pull` |
{% endif %}
| Open the site (for the user) | `make launch`; logged in as admin: `make login` |

## Skills

Reusable iqual engineering knowledge is distributed as Agent Skills through the `iqual-developer` plugin in [`iqual-ch/claude-plugins`](https://github.com/iqual-ch/claude-plugins){% if ai.claude %} (wired up via `.claude/settings.json`){% endif %}. **Don't guess at Drupal- or ICMS-specific implementation details — read the relevant skill first:**

| Skill | Use for |
|---|---|
| `icms-drupal-expert` | Drupal backend conventions in ICMS repos, GraphQL query conventions (`references/graphql.md`), and Blökkli component patterns (`references/blokkli.md`). |
| `icms-update` | Running or debugging a project update, testing an ICMS release candidate, minor/major ICMS upgrades. |
| `drupal-testing` | Writing, placing, and running PHPUnit tests. |
| `drupal-contrib` | Changing a Composer dependency (contrib or iqual package) instead of working around it locally. |

The plugin is the canonical source — it may ship more (or newer) skills than listed here. Project-specific skills, if any, live in `.claude/skills/` in this repository.

## Where code belongs

Project-specific code lives here: custom modules in `drupal/{{ locations['web-root'] }}/modules/custom/`, the client-owned Nuxt app in `frontend/`. If a change is actually about fixing or extending a dependency's own behavior — ICMS packages included — contribute it upstream and consume the update instead of patching it locally (see the `drupal-contrib` skill **before** editing any composer-installed code).
